#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules

# The whole site. Owns the transport and nothing else: each domain is detached
# and brings its own routes, so this file never learns what a thread or a board
# is.
#
# Order matters twice over.
#
# The LANDING PAGE is added first. HttpServer::ResolvePath walks typed children
# in the order they were added and takes the first match, and chess_web.etcs's
# own board_page also answers "/" -- so whichever is attached first owns it.
# Adding landing here, before either lobby is detached, is what makes that
# deterministic rather than a function of which script ran first.
#
# The lobbies are detached AFTER Start, and what makes them find THIS server
# rather than minting a second one that cannot bind 8080 is the verb their own
# web scripts use: `ensure NetworkProvider::HttpServer web`
# (NetworkProvider/scripts/chess_web.etcs). `ensure` takes the name if it
# already resolves and spawns only if it does not; `spawn` ALWAYS creates and
# refuses a name that already resolves (spawn_entity, core/CommandExecutor.h),
# so a subscript that spells it `spawn` fails in exactly the session it was
# written for.
#
# Their own Start calls are no-ops: StartConcrete returns false when a manager
# already exists. Their duplicate FileHtmlPage children are harmless for the
# same first-match reason, just redundant.

spawn NetworkProvider::HttpServer web
web.SetPort(8080)

# Cross-origin isolation, site-wide, which is what makes SharedArrayBuffer --
# and therefore threads -- available at all. /paint is a -pthread wasm build and
# its Workers die on `wasmMemory is undefined` without these two; the same pair
# serve_paint.etcs already carries, moved up here because AddHeader is a property
# of the SERVER and there is one server.
#
# Safe for the pages that came first, and checked rather than assumed: every
# cross-origin url anywhere in www/ is an <a href> (github, youtube,
# anticurrententropy.com), and COEP governs SUBRESOURCES, not navigation. The
# one behaviour this does change is that a link opened in a new tab loses
# window.opener -- which nothing here reads.
web.AddHeader(Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy same-origin)
web.AddHeader(Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy require-corp)

web.spawn(NetworkProvider::StaticHtmlPage landing)
landing.SetHtmlFromFile(ACE_ROOT/scripts/www/index.html)

# Everything else is disk layout as url layout: /chess.html, /forum.html,
# /whitepaper.html. One page type, no per-document entity, and adding a
# document is copying a file rather than editing this script.
web.spawn(NetworkProvider::FileHtmlPage tree)
tree.LoadFromDisk(ACE_ROOT/scripts/www)
tree.ListPaths()

# ── /paint ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The paint page is a SECOND SELF-CONTAINED SITE: its own index.html, its own
# modules.json, ~9 MB of wasm. MountTree gives it a prefix of its own, which is
# what keeps the two index.html files from landing on the same name -- flat, the
# winner would be attach order, the same fragility the "/" note above has to
# explain. Every url inside the page is relative, so it does not learn it was
# mounted; its one absolute link, href="/", now goes where it reads like it goes.
# Relative is also why the address is /paint/ WITH the slash: from /paint the
# browser resolves "modules.json" to /modules.json. The server answers the bare
# spelling with a 301 to the slashed one rather than with the page
# (FileHtmlPage::ResolveConcrete), so either address works and the page's
# fetches always land under the prefix.
#
# Mounted from PaintProvider's own www/ rather than copied into this repo: the
# page is that module's, and a copy here is a second thing to keep current.
tree.MountTree(paint ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/www)

# The one copy of the browser runtime: `ace wasm make` writes bin/wasm/ and
# nothing else does (Makefile, WASM_DIR, on why it is its own directory and why
# a page never holds a copy).
tree.MountTree(wasm ACE_ROOT/bin/wasm)

# The scripts the page stages into the browser FS, each at the path it is
# fetched from (www/modules.json is the source of truth for this list, and
# serve_paint.etcs mounts the same seven at the root of its own server). A name
# the page asks for and this does not mount is a 404 -- and the one that matters
# is render_frames.etcs, the frame pump: losing it leaves a black canvas on a
# runtime that is otherwise working perfectly.
tree.MountFile(paint/paint_routed_pointer.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_routed_pointer.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_toolbar.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_toolbar.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_wheel.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_wheel.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_menu.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_menu.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_layers.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_layers.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_import.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_import.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_visitors.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_visitors.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_eye.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_eye.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_cell_arrow.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_cell_arrow.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_layer_row.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_layer_row.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_page_row.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_page_row.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_anim.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_anim.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_anim_row.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_anim_row.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_visitor_row.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/PaintProvider/scripts/paint_visitor_row.etcs)
tree.MountFile(paint/RenderProvider/scripts/render_frames.etcs ACE_ROOT/modules/RenderProvider/scripts/render_frames.etcs)

# The terminal view, from ShellProvider's own page rather than a copy of it.
# Mounted at "shell", which is what the paint page's iframe points at; the MIME
# comes from the DISK name, so an extensionless url still serves text/html.
tree.MountFile(paint/shell ACE_ROOT/modules/ShellProvider/scripts/www/index.html)

# Printed again after the paint mounts, not only after LoadFromDisk: this is the
# fastest way to catch a staging mistake, and every name added above is one the
# page will ask for.
tree.ListPaths()

# The tar-pit: a self-registering, gate-level filter that catches
# bot-scan-shaped paths (.env, wp-admin, .php, ...) and answers them with a
# deliberately slow 404 instead of routing them anywhere real -- see
# TarpitNode.h for why it lives here as its own entity rather than a flag on
# HttpServer or ConnectionManager.
spawn NetworkProvider::TarpitNode tarpit
tarpit.LoadDefaultTarpitPatterns()

# AddHandler @tarpit Request @tarpit Filter registers the tar-pit as a
# FILTERED gate-level consumer -- ConnectionManager::dispatchToSubscribers
# tries every filtered subscriber before falling back to unfiltered ones, so
# a scan-shaped path is caught here and never reaches web's own Serve.
#
# AddHandler @web Serve is NOT redundant with what Start does automatically
# -- it looks identical to the implicit default (StartConcrete registers
# web's own Serve when handlers_ is empty), but the moment ANY handler is
# added, handlers_ stops being empty and that implicit default is skipped.
# Without this second line, the tar-pit would be the ONLY registered
# consumer and every real request would find no unfiltered fallback and be
# dropped. Declaring it explicitly here is what keeps that fallback alive
# now that a filtered handler exists at all.
web.AddHandler(@tarpit Request @tarpit Filter)
web.AddHandler(@web Serve)

web.Start()
web.IsStarted()

detach ChessProvider/scripts/chess_lobby.etcs
detach forum_lobby.etcs

# THE PAINT SESSION HOST, on this server. The page's share button talks to
# /art on its own origin (defaultNode in PaintProvider's www/index.html), and
# without this line nothing answers there: "[etcs] share: no answer from
# .../art" is exactly that. paint_lobby.etcs ensures `web` and adds the route,
# the same way the chess lobby joins -- after Start, for the reason above.
detach PaintProvider/scripts/paint_lobby.etcs

# http://localhost:8080/